@startuml seq-uc6-track-applications
title UC6 Track My Applications: sequence (success path)

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
autonumber

actor Adopter
participant "MyApplicationsView" as View
participant "TrackApplicationsController" as Controller
participant "TrackApplicationsInteractor\n<<TrackApplicationsInputBoundary>>" as Interactor
participant "FileApplicationDataAccessObject\n<<TrackApplicationsDataAccessInterface>>" as AppDAO
participant "pet data access\n<<TrackApplicationsPetDataAccessInterface>>" as PetDAO
participant "TrackApplicationsPresenter\n<<TrackApplicationsOutputBoundary>>" as Presenter
participant "TrackApplicationsViewModel" as VM

Adopter -> View : opens My Applications\n(or clicks Refresh)
View -> Controller : execute(adopterId)
Controller -> Interactor : execute(new TrackApplicationsInputData(adopterId))

Interactor -> AppDAO : getApplicationsByAdopter(adopterId)
AppDAO --> Interactor : List<Application>
loop for each application
  Interactor -> PetDAO : getPetName(petId)
  PetDAO --> Interactor : pet name\n(or "(pet no longer listed)" if it fails)
  Interactor -> Interactor : new ApplicationSummary(id, petName,\nsubmittedAt, status, adminNote)
end

Interactor -> Presenter : prepareSuccessView(\nnew TrackApplicationsOutputData(summaries))
loop for each summary
  Presenter -> Presenter : new ApplicationRow(petName, date,\nstatus, note or "(no note from the shelter yet)")
end
Presenter -> VM : state.setRows(rows), state.setMessage(...)\nnotifyStateChanged()
VM -> View : stateChanged()
View --> Adopter : table with pet, date submitted and status

Adopter -> View : selects a row
View --> Adopter : shows the shelter's note\n(read from the view model, no use case call)

note over Interactor, Presenter
  If the adopter is not logged in or the applications
  cannot be loaded, the interactor calls prepareFailView(message).
end note

@enduml
